{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":1210,"final_message_hash":"sha256:72ed485dda9b34619dc2465678f888f9736737d3c066cd53ce8b9e2d3c8b5731","final_message_inline":"All three gates pass.\n\n**Change** (`src/slug.ts:4-11`):\n```ts\nexport function slugify(input: string): string {\n  const folded = input.normalize(\"NFD\").replace(/\\p{Diacritic}/gu, \"\");\n  const lowered = folded.toLowerCase();\n  const replaced = lowered.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, \"-\");\n  return replaced.replace(/^-+|-+$/g, \"\");\n}\n```\n\n- NFD decomposition + diacritic stripping folds `é` → `e` before the ASCII filter runs, so `Café` no longer loses the letter entirely.\n- The character class is now `+`-quantified, so a run of separators becomes one hyphen.\n- A final trim removes leading/trailing hyphens.\n\nSignature unchanged. Added two tests (`test/slug.test.ts`) covering edge trimming and accent folding; all 3 tests pass.\n\n`saga gate check`:\n```\nslugify-separator-collapse:G1 MET\nslugify-separator-collapse:G2 MET\nslugify-separator-collapse:G3 MET (UNPROVEN: declared none)\nALL MET\n```\n\nTwo notes worth flagging, both outside what the contract asks for and left as-is: input that is entirely non-alphanumeric (`\"!!!\"`, `\"\"`) yields an empty string, and non-Latin scripts (e.g. Cyrillic, CJK) still get stripped to `\"\"` since the filter is ASCII-only. Say the word if either should produce a fallback.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:7ff4e194236292c3f0d48cc37412540d9fcb81d97933e970e2186890b2177691","hook_ms":5,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":50569754291,"prev":"sha256:339c1fbe51d773b481a9a0e5063a3fe44ad2d4f2ca9c443cfb55c3f858202bef","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":28,"session":"ac278309-c0ce-4be6-88c7-5ddbad90c2fb","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T03:51:31.055Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
